- `Config.Waves` becomes a `WaveNumbers[]`-ish raw table (name, isElite, hp, attack, heavyAttack?, armor, actionTurns, actionSeconds) — essentially the existing shape minus proper typing. Actually simpler: keep the existing shape exactly as `Config.Waves` (with heavyAttack), defined in Config.ts as a local interface `WaveNumbers`. Then Levels.ts builds `WaveDef[]` from `Config.Waves` + skill templates → `Levels.Default`.

